# project: erp-finance-migration

// Streak of consecutive clean month-end closes (reset on any discrepancy).
VAR clean_closes = 0
// Months spent in parallel running (monotonic).
VAR months_parallel = 0
// Parallel-running budget in months; three quarters by default, CFO can extend.
VAR parallel_budget = 9

-> configure_and_load

=== configure_and_load ===
Configure the new finance system and load historical data from the legacy ERP.
Done when configuration is signed off and historical balances tie out in the new system.
* [Historical data loaded and tied out] -> month_end_close

=== month_end_close ===
Run the month-end close in both systems: legacy ERP and the new finance system produce parallel ledgers for the same period.
~ months_parallel += 1
+ [Both closes complete] -> reconcile

=== reconcile ===
The controller reconciles the two ledgers for this period and records the reconciliation evidence.
+ [Ledgers match, clean close] @human -> record_clean_close
+ [Discrepancy found] @human -> root_cause

=== record_clean_close ===
Log a clean close; the cutover streak requires three consecutive clean month-end closes.
~ clean_closes += 1
+ {clean_closes >= 3} [Three consecutive clean closes] -> audit_review
+ {clean_closes < 3 and months_parallel < parallel_budget} [Streak building, run next month] ~loop~ -> month_end_close
+ {clean_closes < 3 and months_parallel >= parallel_budget} [Parallel running past budget] -> cfo_program_review

=== root_cause ===
Chase the root cause of the discrepancy and fix it in config, mappings or process.
Any discrepancy resets the clean-close streak to zero.
~ clean_closes = 0
+ {months_parallel < parallel_budget} [Root cause fixed, resume parallel running] ~loop~ -> month_end_close
+ {months_parallel >= parallel_budget} [Parallel running past budget] -> cfo_program_review

=== audit_review ===
External auditors review the reconciliation evidence for the three clean closes.
+ [Auditors accept the evidence] @human -> cutover_approval
+ [Auditors raise findings, back to parallel running] @human ~loop~ -> month_end_close

=== cutover_approval ===
The CFO makes the cutover go/no-go call on the audited evidence.
+ [CFO approves cutover] @human -> cutover_window
+ [CFO sends us back to parallel running] @human ~loop~ -> month_end_close

=== cutover_window ===
Cutover may happen only between fiscal quarters. Hold at the approved state until the quarter boundary; keep parallel closes running in the meantime.
+ [At the fiscal quarter boundary, go] @human -> execute_cutover
+ [Mid-quarter, keep running parallel until the boundary] @human ~loop~ -> month_end_close

=== execute_cutover ===
Cut over: the new finance system becomes the system of record; the legacy ERP is switched to read-only.
* [Cutover executed cleanly] -> hypercare

=== hypercare ===
One quarter of hypercare on the new system with the legacy ERP available read-only for reference and fallback lookups.
* [Hypercare quarter complete, no open blockers] -> archive_legacy

=== archive_legacy ===
Archive the legacy ERP: preserve data for retention requirements and decommission the system.
-> END

=== cfo_program_review ===
Parallel running has dragged past its budget of three quarters. The CFO decides how the programme proceeds.
+ [Extend parallel running] @human -> extend_program
+ [Descope to core modules only] @human -> descope_core
+ [Abort, fall back to the legacy system] @human -> abort_rollback

=== extend_program ===
Extend the parallel-running budget by one quarter and continue.
~ parallel_budget += 3
+ [Resume parallel running] ~loop~ -> month_end_close

=== descope_core ===
Reduce migration scope to core modules only; reconfigure the new system and restart the clean-close streak for the reduced scope.
~ clean_closes = 0
~ parallel_budget += 3
+ [Core-only scope live, resume parallel running] ~loop~ -> month_end_close

=== abort_rollback ===
Abort the migration: the legacy ERP remains the system of record, the new system is stood down, and lessons learned are written up.
-> END
